{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1530261094,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMzY5MTA0ODE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2680","origin":"github"},"title":"Interoperability with GIN-hosting","message":"Datasets hosted with/at GIN https://web.gin.g-node.org should be working nicely with DataLad. However, there are a few things that needs to polish:\n\n- the GIN webUI only offers \"GIN\" and \"SSH\" access (not sure if anonymous HTTP is intentionally unavailable). This means that DataLad users need to registere, generate, and upload an SSH key to be able to `datalad install` from GIN. That seems needlessly complicated, but we might not be able to do anything about it at our end.\n\n- the \"public\" datasets use datacite as metadata standard (dataset-level), but in the YAML file format flavor. At present DataLad only understands the XML flavor.\n\n- some datasets contain the actual data files as ZIP archives (e.g. https://web.gin.g-node.org/bendalab/Henninger2017_electrosensory), maye we can have a helper that sifts through such a dataset, and unpacks the archives (in the spirit of add-archive).","files":null}]}